A command whose a.go and b.go each hold a string literal, both written at the same
byte and rendered by a line directive at the same position of main.go. One spells
alpha and the other bravo, so each lowers its function's finding to possible.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- a.go --
package main

//line main.go:20:1
var x = "alpha"
-- b.go --
package main

//line main.go:20:1
var y = "bravo"
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(x, y) }

func alpha() {}

func bravo() {}
